Also note the sort comparison uses string `<` which is byte-wise — fine, deterministic. But two ops with different raw bytes that trim to the same... TrimSpace trims Unicode whitespace; that's the specified behavior ("忽略首尾空白"). After trimming, byte comparison must be exact.

